# Can't Buy Me Love, intro (figure 45.1): six bars, elided with the start of the verse.
# The melody outlines the C-major triad over minor chords; Pollack notes the d and G are really
# eleventh and thirteenth chords (typed as plain d and G, kept so).
# The "CEG" before the first bar is a three-note pickup (one beat each, as the rhythm isn't marked);
# in bar 4 the same CEG follows the E, four equal events. The last bar is the verse's downbeat C;
# Pollack types no melody there.
#? Melody octave (C4 up to G4) is a guess; Paul may sing it an octave higher.
